      "title": "How this demo works: Manual tuning",
      "pos": [
        380,
        850
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        280
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Manual tuning\n\nUse image for: manual tuning\nReference: krea-reference-examples/slot2_style_reference.png\nStrength: 0.42\n\nManual mode lets the user decide exactly what the image contributes. This demo borrows palette and finish without borrowing the abstract source shapes: palette wash destroys the source's structure before Krea studies it, so 'Shape copied' can stay live (0.8) and carry the look. On Krea 2 'Overall style reach' has no effect (the model provides no pooled channel) - keep 'Shape copied' alive instead."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
